# Legacy URLs from the previous (Astro) build.
#
# 301, not 302: a 302 tells Google the old URL is still the canonical one, so the
# stale pre-2026 pages stayed in the index instead of passing their equity to /.
# Cloudflare Pages defaults to 302 when the status code is omitted — it was.
#
# NOTE: the www.salonforge.com -> salonforge.com 301 CANNOT live in this file.
# Cloudflare Pages _redirects only accepts a file path as [source]; domain-level
# redirects are explicitly unsupported
# (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/ — "Domain-level
# redirects ❌"). That one needs a Bulk Redirect or a Redirect Rule in the dashboard.
#
# Format: [source] [destination] [code]
/services / 301
/marketing-automation / 301
/live-chat / 301
/lead-generation / 301
